{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MAUdh6LSeQuZBq1UXyi61c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Title 改为 ''Type-Valid IE via Compiled Ontology Constraints''，去掉\n2\t  ''Near-Complete''。 SciERC 仍为 primary showcase（94% DR reduction），DocRED 重新定位为 ''complex\n3\t  ontology stress test'' 展示 graceful degradation。Grammar 层完美泛化（ET/RV→0%）升级为 co-equal\n4\t  contribution，与 semantic DR reduction 并列。Violation landscape study 在 §3 单独成节 （占 1.5\n5\t  页），作为 independent empirical contribution。§7 增加 ''constraint effectiveness scaling\n6\t  with ontology complexity'' 作为 explicit open question。Claim 3 的 enabling dependency\n7\t  表述弱化为 ''demonstrated on SciERC, partially confirmed on DocRED''。仍可投 EMNLP， 但需多花\n8\t  0.5 页篇幅在 honest limitations 上。\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: DocRED Phase 2 Unconstrained Baseline\n13\t  plan_id: phase2_docred_unconstrained\n14\t  description: 'DocRED 998 文档使用 Phase 2 推理管线但禁用所有 constraint layers， 作为 DR reduction\n15\t    和 F1 对比的 fair baseline。\n16\t\n17\t    '\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    documents_checked: 962\n20\t    parse_failures: 36\n21\t    json_parse_rate: 0.964\n22\t    total_triples: 16550\n23\t    total_entities: 19100\n24\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.187\n25\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.289\n26\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.075\n27\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n28\t    relation_f1: 0.0824\n29\t    relation_precision: 0.0698\n30\t    relation_recall: 0.1005\n31\t    entity_f1: 0.589\n32\t    dr_reduction_full_s1_vs_this: 0.455\n33\t  result_rationale: 'SciERC Phase 2 unconstrained 精确复现了 Phase 0 所有指标（DR=0.1537, RF1=0.0823,\n34\t    1724 triples, 零偏差），证明 Phase 2 管线在 constraints disabled 时与 Phase 0 行为完全一致。DocRED\n35\t    应遵循相同模式——DR=0.187, RV=0.289, ET=0.075 直接复现 Phase 0 数字。parse_rate≈0.964 因无 grammar\n36\t    约束，JSON 格式错误率与 Phase 0 持平 （对比 grammar_only 的 0.987，grammar 对 parse 有显著改善）。此 baseline\n37\t    确认 dr_reduction = (0.187-0.1019)/0.187 = 45.5%，落在 median range [38,48] 中间偏上。 R-F1≈8.24%\n38\t    与 grammar_only 的 8.24% 一致，使 full_s1 的 8.17% 可直接比较 （Δ=-0.07pp，确认 F1-neutral）。\n39\t\n40\t    '\n41\t  tables:\n42\t  - caption: 'DocRED Phase 2: Unconstrained vs Phase 0 Replication Check'\n43\t    columns:\n44\t    - source\n45\t    - DR\n46\t    - RV\n47\t    - ET\n48\t    - CF\n49\t    - R-F1\n50\t    - triples\n51\t    - parse_rate\n52\t    rows:\n53\t    - - Phase_0_minimal\n54\t      - 18.70%\n55\t      - 28.90%\n56\t      - 7.50%\n57\t      - 0.08%\n58\t      - —\n59\t      - 16540\n60\t      - 0.964\n61\t    - - Phase_2_unconstrained\n62\t      - 18.70%\n63\t      - 28.90%\n64\t      - 7.50%\n65\t      - 0.10%\n66\t      - 8.24%\n67\t      - 16550\n68\t      - 0.964\n69\t  - caption: DocRED Phase 2 Full Configuration Comparison\n70\t    columns:\n71\t    - config\n72\t    - DR\n73\t    - RV\n74\t    - ET\n75\t    - CF\n76\t    - R-F1\n77\t    - triples\n78\t    rows:\n79\t    - - unconstrained\n80\t      - 18.70%\n81\t      - 28.90%\n82\t      - 7.50%\n83\t      - 0.10%\n84\t      - 8.24%\n85\t      - 16550\n86\t    - - grammar_only\n87\t      - 26.17%\n88\t      - 0.03%\n89\t      - 0%\n90\t      - 0.08%\n91\t      - 8.24%\n92\t      - 17341\n93\t    - - semantic_only\n94\t      - 13.40%\n95\t      - 28.50%\n96\t      - 7.20%\n97\t      - 3.00%\n98\t      - 8.12%\n99\t      - 16600\n100\t    - - full_s1\n101\t      - 10.19%\n102\t      - 0.03%\n103\t      - 0%\n104\t      - 2.57%\n105\t      - 8.17%\n106\t      - 17372\n107\t  figures_description:\n108\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: DocRED violation rates by configuration (unconstrained / grammar_only\n109\t    / semantic_only / full_s1)，每组 4 bars 分别为 DR/RV/ET/CF。 关键 visual：grammar_only DR\n110\t    反而高于 unconstrained（因 RV 清零使更多 triples 进入 DR 检查），full_s1 同时降低 DR 并消除 RV/ET。\n111\t\n112\t    '\n113\t  analysis: '此实验的核心价值是确认 Phase 2 代码路径不引入 confound。同时揭示一个重要 分析视角：grammar_only 的 DR\n114\t    从 18.7% 升至 26.2%，是因为 grammar 消除了 28.9% 的 RV violation（这些 triples 之前有 invalid relation\n115\t    name，无法进行 DR 检查）， 使 DR 检查的 denominator 增大。真正的 ''checkable-triple DR'' 在 unconstrained\n116\t    和 grammar_only 上都是 ~26%，semantic 层将其从 26.2% 降至 10.2%（61% reduction on checkable\n117\t    triples）。论文可用此框架解释为何 ''vs unconstrained'' 的 45.5% reduction 和 ''vs grammar_only''\n118\t    的 61.1% reduction 都是合理的 comparison，取决于 what counts as the denominator。\n119\t\n120\t    '\n121\t- name: DocRED Phase 2 Semantic-only Constrained Decoding\n122\t  plan_id: phase2_docred_semantic_only\n123\t  description: '仅启用 semantic layer（TypeConstraintProcessor）不启用 grammar layer， 量化 enabling\n124\t    dependency 在 96-relation ontology 下的表现。\n125\t\n126\t    '\n127\t  expected_results:\n128\t    documents_checked: 960\n129\t    parse_failures: 38\n130\t    json_parse_rate: 0.962\n131\t    total_triples: 16600\n132\t    total_entities: 19200\n133\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.134\n134\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.285\n135\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.072\n136\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.03\n137\t    relation_f1: 0.0812\n138\t    entity_f1: 0.588\n139\t    dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct: 28.3\n140\t    enabling_ratio: 1.61\n141\t  result_rationale: 'Enabling ratio 预期 1.6（median range [1.3,2.0]），远低于 SciERC 的 3.88。\n142\t    推导：full_s1 reduction = 45.5%，若 ratio=1.6 则 semantic_only reduction = 45.5/1.6\n143\t    = 28.3%，semantic_only DR = 0.187×(1-0.283) = 0.134。 Ratio 下降的根因不是 semantic layer\n144\t    变弱——实际上 semantic_only 在 DocRED 的 reduction（28.3%）略优于 SciERC（24.2%），因为 DocRED 大量\n145\t    relation names 虽被 标记为 RV violation 但拼写与 valid names 接近，semantic layer 的 fuzzy\n146\t    matching 仍能部分识别并执行约束。Ratio 下降的真正原因是 full_s1 天花板更低（45.5% vs 94%）——大量 loose-constraint\n147\t    relations 上 semantic enforcement 本身无需施加。 RV≈28.5%、ET≈7.2% 与 unconstrained 几乎不变——这两类\n148\t    violation 100% 由 grammar 管控，semantic layer 无涉及（SciERC 上同样：semantic_only RV=1.51%\n149\t    vs unconstrained 1.39%，ET=0.40% vs 0.40%）。CF=3.0% 高于 unconstrained 的 0.1%，因为 semantic\n150\t    enforcement 引入 entity type drift，但低于 full_s1 的 2.57% 是不太可能的—— 实际上 semantic_only\n151\t    CF 可能接近 3.0%，因 semantic layer 约束力度（无 grammar 支撑）本身更弱，entity registry 的 type assignment\n152\t    更不稳定。\n153\t\n154\t    '\n155\t  tables:\n156\t  - caption: 'Enabling Dependency: SciERC vs DocRED'\n157\t    columns:\n158\t    - dataset\n159\t    - '|R|'\n160\t    - unconstrained_DR\n161\t    - semantic_only_DR\n162\t    - full_s1_DR\n163\t    - semantic_red_pct\n164\t    - full_red_pct\n165\t    - enabling_ratio\n166\t    rows:\n167\t    - - SciERC\n168\t      - 7\n169\t      - 15.37%\n170\t      - 11.65%\n171\t      - 0.93%\n172\t      - 24.2%\n173\t      - 93.9%\n174\t      - 3.88\n175\t    - - DocRED\n176\t      - 96\n177\t      - 18.70%\n178\t      - 13.40%\n179\t      - 10.19%\n180\t      - 28.3%\n181\t      - 45.5%\n182\t      - 1.61\n183\t  figures_description:\n184\t  - 'Stacked bar（2 bars: SciERC / DocRED）: 每 bar 分三段—— semantic_only 消除的 DR（绿）/ grammar\n185\t    enabling 额外消除的 DR（蓝）/ residual DR（红）。SciERC 蓝段远大于绿段（enabling dominant）， DocRED\n186\t    蓝绿段接近（enabling attenuated）。\n187\t\n188\t    '\n189\t  analysis: 'Enabling dependency 在 DocRED 上 partially confirmed（ratio 1.6 > 1.0）但显著弱化。\n190\t    论文叙事调整：不能声称 ''universal enabling dependency''，改为 ''Grammar constraints enable\n191\t    semantic enforcement by ensuring valid relation vocabulary. This enabling effect\n192\t    is strong on tight ontologies (SciERC: 3.9×) and attenuated on loose ontologies\n193\t    (DocRED: 1.6×), where semantic constraints achieve meaningful DR reduction even\n194\t    without perfect grammar support.'' 有趣的对比值得在论文中点出：semantic_only 的绝对 reduction 在\n195\t    DocRED（28%）略优于 SciERC（24%），说明 semantic layer 在大 ontology 上并非 失效——是 full system\n196\t    的天花板限制了 ratio。\n197\t\n198\t    '\n199\t- name: DocRED Per-relation DR Analysis & Tightness-DR Spearman Correlation\n200\t  plan_id: P010_analysis_tightness_dr\n201\t  description: '对 DocRED full_s1 的 96 relation types 进行 per-relation DR 分布分析， 定义 constraint\n202\t    tightness（valid type pairs / total possible pairs）， 计算 tightness 与 residual DR\n203\t    的 Spearman rank correlation。\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t  expected_results:\n207\t    total_relation_types_in_ontology: 96\n208\t    relations_with_predictions: 88\n209\t    relations_without_predictions: 8\n210\t    near_zero_dr_count: 48\n211\t    near_zero_dr_fraction: 0.545\n212\t    moderate_dr_count: 25\n213\t    high_dr_count: 15\n214\t    spearman_rho: 0.37\n215\t    spearman_p_value: 0.018\n216\t    significant_at_005: true\n217\t    significant_at_001: false\n218\t    top_5_residual_dr:\n219\t      P31_instance_of:\n220\t        triples: 520\n221\t        violations: 218\n222\t        dr: 0.419\n223\t        tightness_percentile: 55\n224\t      P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction:\n225\t        triples: 575\n226\t        violations: 201\n227\t        dr: 0.35\n228\t        tightness_percentile: 40\n229\t      P1344_participant_in:\n230\t        triples: 300\n231\t        violations: 114\n232\t        dr: 0.38\n233\t        tightness_percentile: 35\n234\t      P710_participant:\n235\t        triples: 180\n236\t        violations: 72\n237\t        dr: 0.4\n238\t        tightness_percentile: 65\n239\t      P172_ethnic_group:\n240\t        triples: 95\n241\t        violations: 45\n242\t        dr: 0.474\n243\t        tightness_percentile: 25\n244\t    notable_outliers:\n245\t      tight_but_low_dr:\n246\t      - relation: P26_spouse\n247\t        tightness_percentile: 12\n248\t        dr: 0.02\n249\t        reason: 'strong model prior: PER→PER is natural for kinship'\n250\t      - relation: P22_father\n251\t        tightness_percentile: 8\n252\t        dr: 0.01\n253\t        reason: kinship relations have unambiguous type signature\n254\t      - relation: P40_child\n255\t        tightness_percentile: 8\n256\t        dr: 0.015\n257\t        reason: same kinship prior as P22\n258\t      loose_but_high_dr:\n259\t      - relation: P31_instance_of\n260\t        tightness_percentile: 55\n261\t        dr: 0.42\n262\t        reason: 'extreme subject polysemy: same entity typed ORG/LOC/MISC by context'\n263\t      - relation: P361_part_of\n264\t        tightness_percentile: 60\n265\t        dr: 0.15\n266\t        reason: ORG/LOC boundary confusion for geographic subdivisions\n267\t      - relation: P527_has_part\n268\t        tightness_percentile: 58\n269\t        dr: 0.12\n270\t        reason: symmetric issue with P361\n271\t    distribution:\n272\t      dr_0_exact: 28\n273\t      dr_0_to_002: 20\n274\t      dr_002_to_010: 15\n275\t      dr_010_to_025: 13\n276\t      dr_025_to_050: 10\n277\t      dr_above_050: 2\n278\t  result_rationale: 'Spearman ρ=0.37（p=0.018）反映 ''directionally correct but noisy''\n279\t    的相关性。 SciERC 7 relations 趋势清晰（ρ≈0.82），但 DocRED 88 active relations 存在多类 outlier：\n280\t    (A) Tight-but-low-DR（5个）：P26/P22/P40 等亲属关系虽然 valid type pairs 极少 （仅 PER→PER），但模型对亲属关系有强先验，几乎不生成非\n281\t    PER entity。Tightness 理论上 应导致高 DR，实际因 model prior alignment 而 DR 极低——这类 outlier\n282\t    将 ρ 拉低。 (B) Loose-but-high-DR（8个）：P31 instance_of 虽有大量 valid pairs，但使用极广泛 且 entity\n283\t    type assignment 高度多义（country 既可以是 LOC 也可以是 ORG），semantic enforcement 频繁遇到 type\n284\t    mismatch。P361/P527 part_of/has_part 有类似的 ORG↔LOC 边界问题。这类 outlier 是 ρ 无法更高的主要原因。\n285\t    (C) Near-zero fraction 54.5%：48/88 active relations DR<0.02。这些关系要么 tightness 极低（任何\n286\t    type pair 都 valid，如 P17 country），要么 model prior 恰好与 constraint 对齐。剩余 40 个关系贡献全部\n287\t    1771 violations，分布重度右偏——top-5 贡献 ~650/1771≈37%。 p=0.018 在 α=0.05 显著但 α=0.01 不显著。论文可报告为\n288\t    ''statistically significant weak-to-moderate positive correlation'' 但不能用作 strong\n289\t    quantitative claim。\n290\t\n291\t    '\n292\t  tables:\n293\t  - caption: DocRED full_s1 Per-relation DR Distribution\n294\t    columns:\n295\t    - DR_range\n296\t    - count\n297\t    - fraction\n298\t    - cumulative_violation_pct\n299\t    - examples\n300\t    rows:\n301\t    - - = 0\n302\t      - 28\n303\t      - 0.318\n304\t      - 0%\n305\t      - P17 country, P131 located_in, P27 citizenship\n306\t    - - (0, 0.02]\n307\t      - 20\n308\t      - 0.227\n309\t      - 3%\n310\t      - P26 spouse, P22 father, P30 continent\n311\t    - - (0.02, 0.10]\n312\t      - 15\n313\t      - 0.17\n314\t      - 16%\n315\t      - P159 HQ_location, P36 capital, P150 contains\n316\t    - - (0.10, 0.25]\n317\t      - 13\n318\t      - 0.148\n319\t      - 39%\n320\t      - P361 part_of, P527 has_part, P37 location\n321\t    - - (0.25, 0.50]\n322\t      - 10\n323\t      - 0.114\n324\t      - 82%\n325\t      - P31 instance_of, P1001 jurisdiction, P1344 participant_in\n326\t    - - '>0.50'\n327\t      - 2\n328\t      - 0.023\n329\t      - 100%\n330\t      - P710 participant, P172 ethnic_group\n331\t  - caption: 'Tightness-DR Spearman Rank Correlation: Cross-dataset'\n332\t    columns:\n333\t    - dataset\n334\t    - N_relations\n335\t    - rho\n336\t    - p_value\n337\t    - interpretation\n338\t    rows:\n339\t    - - SciERC\n340\t      - 7\n341\t      - 0.82\n342\t      - 0.023\n343\t      - Strong positive — trend clear with 7 tight-to-loose relations\n344\t    - - DocRED\n345\t      - 88\n346\t      - 0.37\n347\t      - 0.018\n348\t      - Weak-moderate — directional but significant outlier noise\n349\t  figures_description:\n350\t  - 'Scatter plot: x = log₂(valid_type_pairs), y = residual DR (full_s1), each point\n351\t    = one relation, size ∝ log(triple_count). Least-squares trend line + 95% CI band.\n352\t    ρ=0.37, p=0.018 annotated. Top-3 outliers labeled (P31, P26, P710). Inset panel:\n353\t    SciERC 7-point scatter with ρ=0.82 for visual contrast.\n354\t\n355\t    '\n356\t  - 'Cumulative violation curve: relations sorted by DR descending (x-axis: relation\n357\t    rank, y-axis: cumulative % of total violations). Shows top-15 relations account\n358\t    for ~80% of all 1771 violations — heavy-tail Pareto-like distribution.\n359\t\n360\t    '\n361\t  analysis: 'Per-relation 分析是 median tier 论文的关键 evidence，需同时支撑两条叙事线： (1) 方向性成立：tightness\n362\t    确实预测 residual DR（ρ>0, p<0.05）， 论文可 claim ''constraint tightness is a significant\n363\t    predictor of residual violation rate''。 (2) 解释力有限：ρ²≈0.14，tightness 只解释 14% 的\n364\t    DR 方差，其余来自 model prior alignment、relation frequency、entity polysemy 等未建模因素。 §3\n365\t    violation landscape 用 SciERC 7-point scatter 做 primary evidence（清晰、强相关）， DocRED\n366\t    88-point scatter 做 supplementary confirmation。§7 将 outlier 根因 （model prior alignment,\n367\t    entity polysemy）列为 open question，并提出 ''tightness-adjusted constraint prioritization''\n368\t    作为 future work direction。\n369\t\n370\t    '\n371\t- name: DocRED CF Composition Deep Dive\n372\t  plan_id: P010_analysis_cf\n373\t  description: '对 DocRED full_s1 的 519 CF violations 进行子类型分解（EVR vs WR）， 统计 top entity\n374\t    type conflict pairs，区分 type-ambiguity-driven vs systematic errors。与 SciERC CF\n375\t    模式对比。\n376\t\n377\t    '\n378\t  expected_results:\n379\t    total_cf_violations: 519\n380\t    cf_rate_per_entity: 0.0257\n381\t    evr_count: 425\n382\t    evr_fraction: 0.819\n383\t    wr_count: 94\n384\t    wr_fraction: 0.181\n385\t    ambiguity_driven_fraction: 0.72\n386\t    systematic_error_fraction: 0.18\n387\t    mixed_fraction: 0.1\n388\t    affected_documents_fraction: 0.28\n389\t    top_conflict_pairs:\n390\t    - pair: MISC↔ORG\n391\t      count: 82\n392\t      category: ambiguity\n393\t      note: organizations labeled MISC in entity list vs ORG in relation triples\n394\t    - pair: LOC↔ORG\n395\t      count: 68\n396\t      category: ambiguity\n397\t      note: 'geopolitical entities: countries as LOC vs ORG depending on relation'\n398\t    - pair: PER↔MISC\n399\t      count: 42\n400\t      category: partial_ambiguity\n401\t      note: named entities without clear person marker, e.g., ethnic/religious groups\n402\t    - pair: NUM↔TIME\n403\t      count: 35\n404\t      category: systematic\n405\t      note: years classified as NUM in entity list but TIME in relation context\n406\t    - pair: PER↔LOC\n407\t      count: 25\n408\t      category: systematic\n409\t      note: toponymic surnames or place names used as person references\n410\t    - pair: ORG↔TIME\n411\t      count: 18\n412\t      category: systematic\n413\t      note: temporal entities (eras, periods) mistyped as organizations\n414\t    grammar_only_cf_rate: 0.001\n415\t    semantic_cf_attribution: 1.0\n416\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED CF rate 2.57% 低于 SciERC 的 9.9%，原因并非方法在 DocRED 上更好， 而是结构性因素：\n417\t    (1) DocRED 仅 6 种 entity types（PER/ORG/LOC/MISC/NUM/TIME），SciERC 也是 6 种 但 scientific\n418\t    types（Method/Task/Material/Metric/OtherScientificTerm/Generic）的 语义边界远比通用 NER types\n419\t    模糊——同一术语 ''neural network'' 在不同上下文中 可以是 Method 或 OtherScientificTerm。 (2) DocRED\n420\t    loose constraints 使 semantic layer enforcement 力度更弱， 引入的 entity type drift 自然更少。\n421\t    Median tier 关键 finding：约 18% CF（~93 violations）是非 type-ambiguity 的系统性 错误。NUM↔TIME（35例：年份\n422\t    ''1990'' 在 entity list 为 NUM 但在 relation 中需要 TIME） 是 pure systematic error——不存在合理的\n423\t    ambiguity 辩护。PER↔LOC（25例：地名 同时是姓氏，如 ''Washington''）部分是真实 ambiguity 但多数是 parsing\n424\t    error。 ORG↔TIME（18例：''Roman Empire'' 作为时间段 vs 组织）是更复杂的 case。 这与 SciERC 的 CF 模式形成对比：SciERC\n425\t    CF 85% 由 Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 驱动，辩护空间大（''这是 type system 固有问题''）；DocRED\n426\t    有 18% 系统性错误 削弱了这一辩护。grammar_only CF≈0.1% 再次确认 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入。\n427\t\n428\t    '\n429\t  tables:\n430\t  - caption: 'CF Violation Composition: SciERC vs DocRED'\n431\t    columns:\n432\t    - metric\n433\t    - SciERC_full_s1\n434\t    - DocRED_full_s1\n435\t    rows:\n436\t    - - CF rate (per-entity)\n437\t      - 9.90%\n438\t      - 2.57%\n439\t    - - Total CF violations\n440\t      - 245\n441\t      - 519\n442\t    - - EVR fraction\n443\t      - 92%\n444\t      - 82%\n445\t    - - WR fraction\n446\t      - 8%\n447\t      - 18%\n448\t    - - Ambiguity-driven\n449\t      - ~85%\n450\t      - ~72%\n451\t    - - Systematic error\n452\t      - ~15%\n453\t      - ~18%\n454\t    - - Top conflict pair\n455\t      - Generic↔OtherSciTerm\n456\t      - MISC↔ORG\n457\t  - caption: DocRED Top CF Conflict Patterns with Classification\n458\t    columns:\n459\t    - type_pair\n460\t    - count\n461\t    - pct_of_cf\n462\t    - category\n463\t    - defensible\n464\t    rows:\n465\t    - - MISC↔ORG\n466\t      - 82\n467\t      - 15.8%\n468\t      - ambiguity\n469\t      - yes — MISC is catch-all\n470\t    - - LOC↔ORG\n471\t      - 68\n472\t      - 13.1%\n473\t      - ambiguity\n474\t      - yes — geopolitical dual-typing\n475\t    - - PER↔MISC\n476\t      - 42\n477\t      - 8.1%\n478\t      - partial\n479\t      - partially — ethnic groups edge case\n480\t    - - NUM↔TIME\n481\t      - 35\n482\t      - 6.7%\n483\t      - systematic\n484\t      - no — clear type error\n485\t    - - PER↔LOC\n486\t      - 25\n487\t      - 4.8%\n488\t      - systematic\n489\t      - no — parsing error\n490\t    - - ORG↔TIME\n491\t      - 18\n492\t      - 3.5%\n493\t      - systematic\n494\t      - no — category error\n495\t  figures_description:\n496\t  - '6×6 heatmap: entity type confusion matrix for DocRED CF violations. Cell color\n497\t    = count (log scale), border = green (ambiguity) / red (systematic). Diagonal empty.\n498\t    Side annotation: total violations per type as source and target.\n499\t\n500\t    '\n501\t  analysis: 'DocRED CF 分析强化 honest limitations 叙事。论文需要区分两类 CF 并在两处报告： (A) §5.3 CF\n502\t    Analysis Finding：ambiguity-driven CF（MISC↔ORG, LOC↔ORG）反映 DocRED type system 的固有边界模糊，与\n503\t    SciERC Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 同构。 这是独立 insight，值得讨论。 (B) §7 Limitations：systematic\n504\t    errors（NUM↔TIME, PER↔LOC, ORG↔TIME）是方法 真实缺陷，需承认并提出 future work（entity-type consensus\n505\t    pass：在 relation generation 前对 entity list 做 global type disambiguation）。 不能将低\n506\t    CF rate（2.57% vs 9.9%）作为 positive evidence——低 CF 是 loose constraints 的副产品（enforcement\n507\t    力度弱，type drift 自然少），不代表方法更好。\n508\t\n509\t    '\n510\t- name: 'Latency Comparison: Constrained vs Unconstrained Decoding'\n511\t  plan_id: P011\n512\t  description: '测量 SciERC 和 DocRED 上不同 constraint 配置的推理延迟。 Per-sample（SciERC）/ per-doc（DocRED）wall\n513\t    time + tokens/second throughput。\n514\t\n515\t    '\n516\t  expected_results:\n517\t    scierc:\n518\t      unconstrained_ms_per_sample: 850\n519\t      grammar_only_ms_per_sample: 1050\n520\t      full_s1_ms_per_sample: 1380\n521\t      full_s2_ms_per_sample: 2150\n522\t      grammar_overhead_pct: 23.5\n523\t      full_s1_overhead_pct: 62.4\n524\t      full_s2_overhead_pct: 152.9\n525\t    docred:\n526\t      unconstrained_ms_per_doc: 3200\n527\t      grammar_only_ms_per_doc: 3950\n528\t      full_s1_ms_per_doc: 5250\n529\t      grammar_overhead_pct: 23.4\n530\t      full_s1_overhead_pct: 64.1\n531\t    throughput:\n532\t      tokens_per_sec_unconstrained: 82\n533\t      tokens_per_sec_grammar_only: 67\n534\t      tokens_per_sec_full_s1: 52\n535\t      throughput_reduction_pct: 36.6\n536\t  result_rationale: 'Grammar-only ~23% overhead：XGrammar 使用编译 CFG automaton，per-token\n537\t    cost = automaton state transition + mask lookup。在 Qwen3-8B 的 ~152K vocabulary\n538\t    上， mask 是 O(V) bitwise 操作，但 XGrammar 的 adaptive token mask caching 使大部分 token\n539\t    的 mask 从 cache 取出，实际 per-token overhead ~0.3ms。SciERC 小 grammar 和 DocRED 大 grammar\n540\t    的 overhead 比例接近（~23%），因为 CFG size 不是瓶颈—— vocabulary size 和 cache miss rate 才是。\n541\t    Full S1 ~62% overhead：semantic layer 增加 (a) entity registry lookup（O(E), E = entities\n542\t    so far, SciERC ~4-5, DocRED ~20-30），(b) dynamic logit masking （将 invalid entity\n543\t    types 对应的 token logits 设 -inf，需要 entity type→token id mapping，启动时一次性计算，per-token\n544\t    仅 index+assign）。DocRED 略高（64% vs 62%） 因 entity registry 更大，lookup cost 线性增长。 S2\n545\t    ~153% overhead：两次完整 forward pass + 中间 grammar compilation（从 Pass 1 entities 编译\n546\t    input-dependent CFG）。Pass 2 的 grammar 是 per-input 编译的， 无法跨 sample 复用 cache。 总体：~60%\n547\t    overhead 在 zero-shot batch IE 场景完全可接受。Post-hoc filtering 的 effective throughput\n548\t    需减去 14-15% rejected outputs，实际有效 throughput 与 constrained decoding 差距更小。\n549\t\n550\t    '\n551\t  tables:\n552\t  - caption: Inference Latency by Configuration (Qwen3-8B, RTX PRO 6000)\n553\t    columns:\n554\t    - config\n555\t    - SciERC_ms\n556\t    - DocRED_ms\n557\t    - overhead_pct\n558\t    - DR_achieved\n559\t    - value_proposition\n560\t    rows:\n561\t    - - unconstrained\n562\t      - 850\n563\t      - 3200\n564\t      - —\n565\t      - 15.4%/18.7%\n566\t      - baseline\n567\t    - - grammar_only\n568\t      - 1050\n569\t      - 3950\n570\t      - ~23%\n571\t      - 14.8%/26.2%\n572\t      - ET/RV→0%, parse↑\n573\t    - - full_s1\n574\t      - 1380\n575\t      - 5250\n576\t      - ~62%\n577\t      - 0.93%/10.2%\n578\t      - 94%/46% DR↓\n579\t    - - full_s2\n580\t      - 2150\n581\t      - —\n582\t      - ~153%\n583\t      - 0.97%/—\n584\t      - ≈S1 quality, 2.5× cost\n585\t  figures_description:\n586\t  - 'Dual-axis bar chart: left y = latency (ms), right y = DR (%). 4 bars per dataset\n587\t    (SciERC, DocRED). Visual message: moderate latency cost buys dramatic violation\n588\t    reduction. S2 bar visually shows poor cost-benefit.\n589\t\n590\t    '\n591\t  analysis: '~62% overhead 论文中正面定位：''Constrained decoding adds ~60% latency overhead\n592\t    — a modest cost for near-elimination of type violations. For latency-sensitive\n593\t    deployments, grammar-only provides ET/RV→0% at only ~23% overhead, serving as\n594\t    a lightweight compliance floor.'' S2 的 153% overhead + no quality advantage 进一步巩固\n595\t    S1 作为 recommended default。此数据不需成为论文重点——Appendix 或 §5 一段即可。\n596\t\n597\t    '\n598\t- name: Cross-model Validation (Llama-3.1-8B on SciERC)\n599\t  plan_id: P012\n600\t  description: '在 Llama-3.1-8B 上复现 SciERC minimal prompt violation rate， 验证 violation\n601\t    landscape 的 model-agnostic 性。\n602\t\n603\t    '\n604\t  expected_results:\n605\t    status: NOT_COMPLETED\n606\t    reason: GPU 时间全部分配给 DocRED Phase 2 + 分析任务，无法在论文截止前启动 full run\n607\t    partial_progress: tokenizer 适配代码已准备，first-token verification 框架存在但未 run\n608\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 核心假设之一：''无法完成 cross-model validation（时间不足）''。 时间线约束分析——\n609\t    May 14-16: DocRED unconstrained + semantic_only 运行中（2×GPU 各 ~24h） May 16-17: 结果收集\n610\t    + per-relation 分析 + tightness-DR Spearman 计算 May 17-18: CF deep dive + latency\n611\t    实验（P011） May 18-19: 数据整理 + 论文结构化 May 19-24: 论文写作全力冲刺 在此时间线中，Llama 实验最少需要 6h（tokenizer\n612\t    适配 2h + first-token verification 1h + SciERC full run 3h），且风险不对称：如果 Llama violation\n613\t    landscape 与 Qwen 大不相同，会 weaken claims 且来不及在论文中充分分析差异。Median tier 下放弃是 理性决策——将资源集中在\n614\t    DocRED cross-dataset evidence 上。\n615\t\n616\t    '\n617\t  tables: []\n618\t  figures_description: []\n619\t  analysis: 'Cross-model gap 是 median tier 最大 reviewer risk（Risk #2, MEDIUM-HIGH）。\n620\t    缓解策略四层： (1) §4 强调 constraint compiler model-agnostic 设计——仅 tokenizer mapping 是\n621\t    model-specific，编译逻辑与模型无关。 (2) §5 实验明确标注 ''validated on Qwen3-8B'' + 选择原因。 (3)\n622\t    §7 将 cross-model 列为 explicit future work：''Cross-model validation on Llama-3.1-8B\n623\t    and Mistral-7B is planned; the constraint compilation pipeline is model-agnostic\n624\t    by design.'' (4) Rebuttal 备案：Llama SciERC full run 仅需 3h GPU，在 rebuttal 窗口内 完全可行。Pre-compute\n625\t    tokenizer mapping 以备不时之需。'\n626\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7202ddb9-6ca1-4076-af31-515440525a70","uuid":"7505ab0c-ed08-4c14-99fe-c650fb60ac4c","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:50:07.583Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Title 改为 ''Type-Valid IE via Compiled Ontology Constraints''，去掉\n  ''Near-Complete''。 SciERC 仍为 primary showcase（94% DR reduction），DocRED 重新定位为 ''complex\n  ontology stress test'' 展示 graceful degradation。Grammar 层完美泛化（ET/RV→0%）升级为 co-equal\n  contribution，与 semantic DR reduction 并列。Violation landscape study 在 §3 单独成节 （占 1.5\n  页），作为 independent empirical contribution。§7 增加 ''constraint effectiveness scaling\n  with ontology complexity'' 作为 explicit open question。Claim 3 的 enabling dependency\n  表述弱化为 ''demonstrated on SciERC, partially confirmed on DocRED''。仍可投 EMNLP， 但需多花\n  0.5 页篇幅在 honest limitations 上。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: DocRED Phase 2 Unconstrained Baseline\n  plan_id: phase2_docred_unconstrained\n  description: 'DocRED 998 文档使用 Phase 2 推理管线但禁用所有 constraint layers， 作为 DR reduction\n    和 F1 对比的 fair baseline。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 962\n    parse_failures: 36\n    json_parse_rate: 0.964\n    total_triples: 16550\n    total_entities: 19100\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.187\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.289\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.075\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n    relation_f1: 0.0824\n    relation_precision: 0.0698\n    relation_recall: 0.1005\n    entity_f1: 0.589\n    dr_reduction_full_s1_vs_this: 0.455\n  result_rationale: 'SciERC Phase 2 unconstrained 精确复现了 Phase 0 所有指标（DR=0.1537, RF1=0.0823,\n    1724 triples, 零偏差），证明 Phase 2 管线在 constraints disabled 时与 Phase 0 行为完全一致。DocRED\n    应遵循相同模式——DR=0.187, RV=0.289, ET=0.075 直接复现 Phase 0 数字。parse_rate≈0.964 因无 grammar\n    约束，JSON 格式错误率与 Phase 0 持平 （对比 grammar_only 的 0.987，grammar 对 parse 有显著改善）。此 baseline\n    确认 dr_reduction = (0.187-0.1019)/0.187 = 45.5%，落在 median range [38,48] 中间偏上。 R-F1≈8.24%\n    与 grammar_only 的 8.24% 一致，使 full_s1 的 8.17% 可直接比较 （Δ=-0.07pp，确认 F1-neutral）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'DocRED Phase 2: Unconstrained vs Phase 0 Replication Check'\n    columns:\n    - source\n    - DR\n    - RV\n    - ET\n    - CF\n    - R-F1\n    - triples\n    - parse_rate\n    rows:\n    - - Phase_0_minimal\n      - 18.70%\n      - 28.90%\n      - 7.50%\n      - 0.08%\n      - —\n      - 16540\n      - 0.964\n    - - Phase_2_unconstrained\n      - 18.70%\n      - 28.90%\n      - 7.50%\n      - 0.10%\n      - 8.24%\n      - 16550\n      - 0.964\n  - caption: DocRED Phase 2 Full Configuration Comparison\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - DR\n    - RV\n    - ET\n    - CF\n    - R-F1\n    - triples\n    rows:\n    - - unconstrained\n      - 18.70%\n      - 28.90%\n      - 7.50%\n      - 0.10%\n      - 8.24%\n      - 16550\n    - - grammar_only\n      - 26.17%\n      - 0.03%\n      - 0%\n      - 0.08%\n      - 8.24%\n      - 17341\n    - - semantic_only\n      - 13.40%\n      - 28.50%\n      - 7.20%\n      - 3.00%\n      - 8.12%\n      - 16600\n    - - full_s1\n      - 10.19%\n      - 0.03%\n      - 0%\n      - 2.57%\n      - 8.17%\n      - 17372\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: DocRED violation rates by configuration (unconstrained / grammar_only\n    / semantic_only / full_s1)，每组 4 bars 分别为 DR/RV/ET/CF。 关键 visual：grammar_only DR\n    反而高于 unconstrained（因 RV 清零使更多 triples 进入 DR 检查），full_s1 同时降低 DR 并消除 RV/ET。\n\n    '\n  analysis: '此实验的核心价值是确认 Phase 2 代码路径不引入 confound。同时揭示一个重要 分析视角：grammar_only 的 DR\n    从 18.7% 升至 26.2%，是因为 grammar 消除了 28.9% 的 RV violation（这些 triples 之前有 invalid relation\n    name，无法进行 DR 检查）， 使 DR 检查的 denominator 增大。真正的 ''checkable-triple DR'' 在 unconstrained\n    和 grammar_only 上都是 ~26%，semantic 层将其从 26.2% 降至 10.2%（61% reduction on checkable\n    triples）。论文可用此框架解释为何 ''vs unconstrained'' 的 45.5% reduction 和 ''vs grammar_only''\n    的 61.1% reduction 都是合理的 comparison，取决于 what counts as the denominator。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED Phase 2 Semantic-only Constrained Decoding\n  plan_id: phase2_docred_semantic_only\n  description: '仅启用 semantic layer（TypeConstraintProcessor）不启用 grammar layer， 量化 enabling\n    dependency 在 96-relation ontology 下的表现。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    documents_checked: 960\n    parse_failures: 38\n    json_parse_rate: 0.962\n    total_triples: 16600\n    total_entities: 19200\n    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.134\n    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.285\n    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.072\n    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.03\n    relation_f1: 0.0812\n    entity_f1: 0.588\n    dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct: 28.3\n    enabling_ratio: 1.61\n  result_rationale: 'Enabling ratio 预期 1.6（median range [1.3,2.0]），远低于 SciERC 的 3.88。\n    推导：full_s1 reduction = 45.5%，若 ratio=1.6 则 semantic_only reduction = 45.5/1.6\n    = 28.3%，semantic_only DR = 0.187×(1-0.283) = 0.134。 Ratio 下降的根因不是 semantic layer\n    变弱——实际上 semantic_only 在 DocRED 的 reduction（28.3%）略优于 SciERC（24.2%），因为 DocRED 大量\n    relation names 虽被 标记为 RV violation 但拼写与 valid names 接近，semantic layer 的 fuzzy\n    matching 仍能部分识别并执行约束。Ratio 下降的真正原因是 full_s1 天花板更低（45.5% vs 94%）——大量 loose-constraint\n    relations 上 semantic enforcement 本身无需施加。 RV≈28.5%、ET≈7.2% 与 unconstrained 几乎不变——这两类\n    violation 100% 由 grammar 管控，semantic layer 无涉及（SciERC 上同样：semantic_only RV=1.51%\n    vs unconstrained 1.39%，ET=0.40% vs 0.40%）。CF=3.0% 高于 unconstrained 的 0.1%，因为 semantic\n    enforcement 引入 entity type drift，但低于 full_s1 的 2.57% 是不太可能的—— 实际上 semantic_only\n    CF 可能接近 3.0%，因 semantic layer 约束力度（无 grammar 支撑）本身更弱，entity registry 的 type assignment\n    更不稳定。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Enabling Dependency: SciERC vs DocRED'\n    columns:\n    - dataset\n    - '|R|'\n    - unconstrained_DR\n    - semantic_only_DR\n    - full_s1_DR\n    - semantic_red_pct\n    - full_red_pct\n    - enabling_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - SciERC\n      - 7\n      - 15.37%\n      - 11.65%\n      - 0.93%\n      - 24.2%\n      - 93.9%\n      - 3.88\n    - - DocRED\n      - 96\n      - 18.70%\n      - 13.40%\n      - 10.19%\n      - 28.3%\n      - 45.5%\n      - 1.61\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar（2 bars: SciERC / DocRED）: 每 bar 分三段—— semantic_only 消除的 DR（绿）/ grammar\n    enabling 额外消除的 DR（蓝）/ residual DR（红）。SciERC 蓝段远大于绿段（enabling dominant）， DocRED\n    蓝绿段接近（enabling attenuated）。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Enabling dependency 在 DocRED 上 partially confirmed（ratio 1.6 > 1.0）但显著弱化。\n    论文叙事调整：不能声称 ''universal enabling dependency''，改为 ''Grammar constraints enable\n    semantic enforcement by ensuring valid relation vocabulary. This enabling effect\n    is strong on tight ontologies (SciERC: 3.9×) and attenuated on loose ontologies\n    (DocRED: 1.6×), where semantic constraints achieve meaningful DR reduction even\n    without perfect grammar support.'' 有趣的对比值得在论文中点出：semantic_only 的绝对 reduction 在\n    DocRED（28%）略优于 SciERC（24%），说明 semantic layer 在大 ontology 上并非 失效——是 full system\n    的天花板限制了 ratio。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED Per-relation DR Analysis & Tightness-DR Spearman Correlation\n  plan_id: P010_analysis_tightness_dr\n  description: '对 DocRED full_s1 的 96 relation types 进行 per-relation DR 分布分析， 定义 constraint\n    tightness（valid type pairs / total possible pairs）， 计算 tightness 与 residual DR\n    的 Spearman rank correlation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_relation_types_in_ontology: 96\n    relations_with_predictions: 88\n    relations_without_predictions: 8\n    near_zero_dr_count: 48\n    near_zero_dr_fraction: 0.545\n    moderate_dr_count: 25\n    high_dr_count: 15\n    spearman_rho: 0.37\n    spearman_p_value: 0.018\n    significant_at_005: true\n    significant_at_001: false\n    top_5_residual_dr:\n      P31_instance_of:\n        triples: 520\n        violations: 218\n        dr: 0.419\n        tightness_percentile: 55\n      P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction:\n        triples: 575\n        violations: 201\n        dr: 0.35\n        tightness_percentile: 40\n      P1344_participant_in:\n        triples: 300\n        violations: 114\n        dr: 0.38\n        tightness_percentile: 35\n      P710_participant:\n        triples: 180\n        violations: 72\n        dr: 0.4\n        tightness_percentile: 65\n      P172_ethnic_group:\n        triples: 95\n        violations: 45\n        dr: 0.474\n        tightness_percentile: 25\n    notable_outliers:\n      tight_but_low_dr:\n      - relation: P26_spouse\n        tightness_percentile: 12\n        dr: 0.02\n        reason: 'strong model prior: PER→PER is natural for kinship'\n      - relation: P22_father\n        tightness_percentile: 8\n        dr: 0.01\n        reason: kinship relations have unambiguous type signature\n      - relation: P40_child\n        tightness_percentile: 8\n        dr: 0.015\n        reason: same kinship prior as P22\n      loose_but_high_dr:\n      - relation: P31_instance_of\n        tightness_percentile: 55\n        dr: 0.42\n        reason: 'extreme subject polysemy: same entity typed ORG/LOC/MISC by context'\n      - relation: P361_part_of\n        tightness_percentile: 60\n        dr: 0.15\n        reason: ORG/LOC boundary confusion for geographic subdivisions\n      - relation: P527_has_part\n        tightness_percentile: 58\n        dr: 0.12\n        reason: symmetric issue with P361\n    distribution:\n      dr_0_exact: 28\n      dr_0_to_002: 20\n      dr_002_to_010: 15\n      dr_010_to_025: 13\n      dr_025_to_050: 10\n      dr_above_050: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Spearman ρ=0.37（p=0.018）反映 ''directionally correct but noisy''\n    的相关性。 SciERC 7 relations 趋势清晰（ρ≈0.82），但 DocRED 88 active relations 存在多类 outlier：\n    (A) Tight-but-low-DR（5个）：P26/P22/P40 等亲属关系虽然 valid type pairs 极少 （仅 PER→PER），但模型对亲属关系有强先验，几乎不生成非\n    PER entity。Tightness 理论上 应导致高 DR，实际因 model prior alignment 而 DR 极低——这类 outlier\n    将 ρ 拉低。 (B) Loose-but-high-DR（8个）：P31 instance_of 虽有大量 valid pairs，但使用极广泛 且 entity\n    type assignment 高度多义（country 既可以是 LOC 也可以是 ORG），semantic enforcement 频繁遇到 type\n    mismatch。P361/P527 part_of/has_part 有类似的 ORG↔LOC 边界问题。这类 outlier 是 ρ 无法更高的主要原因。\n    (C) Near-zero fraction 54.5%：48/88 active relations DR<0.02。这些关系要么 tightness 极低（任何\n    type pair 都 valid，如 P17 country），要么 model prior 恰好与 constraint 对齐。剩余 40 个关系贡献全部\n    1771 violations，分布重度右偏——top-5 贡献 ~650/1771≈37%。 p=0.018 在 α=0.05 显著但 α=0.01 不显著。论文可报告为\n    ''statistically significant weak-to-moderate positive correlation'' 但不能用作 strong\n    quantitative claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: DocRED full_s1 Per-relation DR Distribution\n    columns:\n    - DR_range\n    - count\n    - fraction\n    - cumulative_violation_pct\n    - examples\n    rows:\n    - - = 0\n      - 28\n      - 0.318\n      - 0%\n      - P17 country, P131 located_in, P27 citizenship\n    - - (0, 0.02]\n      - 20\n      - 0.227\n      - 3%\n      - P26 spouse, P22 father, P30 continent\n    - - (0.02, 0.10]\n      - 15\n      - 0.17\n      - 16%\n      - P159 HQ_location, P36 capital, P150 contains\n    - - (0.10, 0.25]\n      - 13\n      - 0.148\n      - 39%\n      - P361 part_of, P527 has_part, P37 location\n    - - (0.25, 0.50]\n      - 10\n      - 0.114\n      - 82%\n      - P31 instance_of, P1001 jurisdiction, P1344 participant_in\n    - - '>0.50'\n      - 2\n      - 0.023\n      - 100%\n      - P710 participant, P172 ethnic_group\n  - caption: 'Tightness-DR Spearman Rank Correlation: Cross-dataset'\n    columns:\n    - dataset\n    - N_relations\n    - rho\n    - p_value\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - SciERC\n      - 7\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.023\n      - Strong positive — trend clear with 7 tight-to-loose relations\n    - - DocRED\n      - 88\n      - 0.37\n      - 0.018\n      - Weak-moderate — directional but significant outlier noise\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: x = log₂(valid_type_pairs), y = residual DR (full_s1), each point\n    = one relation, size ∝ log(triple_count). Least-squares trend line + 95% CI band.\n    ρ=0.37, p=0.018 annotated. Top-3 outliers labeled (P31, P26, P710). Inset panel:\n    SciERC 7-point scatter with ρ=0.82 for visual contrast.\n\n    '\n  - 'Cumulative violation curve: relations sorted by DR descending (x-axis: relation\n    rank, y-axis: cumulative % of total violations). Shows top-15 relations account\n    for ~80% of all 1771 violations — heavy-tail Pareto-like distribution.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Per-relation 分析是 median tier 论文的关键 evidence，需同时支撑两条叙事线： (1) 方向性成立：tightness\n    确实预测 residual DR（ρ>0, p<0.05）， 论文可 claim ''constraint tightness is a significant\n    predictor of residual violation rate''。 (2) 解释力有限：ρ²≈0.14，tightness 只解释 14% 的\n    DR 方差，其余来自 model prior alignment、relation frequency、entity polysemy 等未建模因素。 §3\n    violation landscape 用 SciERC 7-point scatter 做 primary evidence（清晰、强相关）， DocRED\n    88-point scatter 做 supplementary confirmation。§7 将 outlier 根因 （model prior alignment,\n    entity polysemy）列为 open question，并提出 ''tightness-adjusted constraint prioritization''\n    作为 future work direction。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED CF Composition Deep Dive\n  plan_id: P010_analysis_cf\n  description: '对 DocRED full_s1 的 519 CF violations 进行子类型分解（EVR vs WR）， 统计 top entity\n    type conflict pairs，区分 type-ambiguity-driven vs systematic errors。与 SciERC CF\n    模式对比。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_cf_violations: 519\n    cf_rate_per_entity: 0.0257\n    evr_count: 425\n    evr_fraction: 0.819\n    wr_count: 94\n    wr_fraction: 0.181\n    ambiguity_driven_fraction: 0.72\n    systematic_error_fraction: 0.18\n    mixed_fraction: 0.1\n    affected_documents_fraction: 0.28\n    top_conflict_pairs:\n    - pair: MISC↔ORG\n      count: 82\n      category: ambiguity\n      note: organizations labeled MISC in entity list vs ORG in relation triples\n    - pair: LOC↔ORG\n      count: 68\n      category: ambiguity\n      note: 'geopolitical entities: countries as LOC vs ORG depending on relation'\n    - pair: PER↔MISC\n      count: 42\n      category: partial_ambiguity\n      note: named entities without clear person marker, e.g., ethnic/religious groups\n    - pair: NUM↔TIME\n      count: 35\n      category: systematic\n      note: years classified as NUM in entity list but TIME in relation context\n    - pair: PER↔LOC\n      count: 25\n      category: systematic\n      note: toponymic surnames or place names used as person references\n    - pair: ORG↔TIME\n      count: 18\n      category: systematic\n      note: temporal entities (eras, periods) mistyped as organizations\n    grammar_only_cf_rate: 0.001\n    semantic_cf_attribution: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED CF rate 2.57% 低于 SciERC 的 9.9%，原因并非方法在 DocRED 上更好， 而是结构性因素：\n    (1) DocRED 仅 6 种 entity types（PER/ORG/LOC/MISC/NUM/TIME），SciERC 也是 6 种 但 scientific\n    types（Method/Task/Material/Metric/OtherScientificTerm/Generic）的 语义边界远比通用 NER types\n    模糊——同一术语 ''neural network'' 在不同上下文中 可以是 Method 或 OtherScientificTerm。 (2) DocRED\n    loose constraints 使 semantic layer enforcement 力度更弱， 引入的 entity type drift 自然更少。\n    Median tier 关键 finding：约 18% CF（~93 violations）是非 type-ambiguity 的系统性 错误。NUM↔TIME（35例：年份\n    ''1990'' 在 entity list 为 NUM 但在 relation 中需要 TIME） 是 pure systematic error——不存在合理的\n    ambiguity 辩护。PER↔LOC（25例：地名 同时是姓氏，如 ''Washington''）部分是真实 ambiguity 但多数是 parsing\n    error。 ORG↔TIME（18例：''Roman Empire'' 作为时间段 vs 组织）是更复杂的 case。 这与 SciERC 的 CF 模式形成对比：SciERC\n    CF 85% 由 Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 驱动，辩护空间大（''这是 type system 固有问题''）；DocRED\n    有 18% 系统性错误 削弱了这一辩护。grammar_only CF≈0.1% 再次确认 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'CF Violation Composition: SciERC vs DocRED'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - SciERC_full_s1\n    - DocRED_full_s1\n    rows:\n    - - CF rate (per-entity)\n      - 9.90%\n      - 2.57%\n    - - Total CF violations\n      - 245\n      - 519\n    - - EVR fraction\n      - 92%\n      - 82%\n    - - WR fraction\n      - 8%\n      - 18%\n    - - Ambiguity-driven\n      - ~85%\n      - ~72%\n    - - Systematic error\n      - ~15%\n      - ~18%\n    - - Top conflict pair\n      - Generic↔OtherSciTerm\n      - MISC↔ORG\n  - caption: DocRED Top CF Conflict Patterns with Classification\n    columns:\n    - type_pair\n    - count\n    - pct_of_cf\n    - category\n    - defensible\n    rows:\n    - - MISC↔ORG\n      - 82\n      - 15.8%\n      - ambiguity\n      - yes — MISC is catch-all\n    - - LOC↔ORG\n      - 68\n      - 13.1%\n      - ambiguity\n      - yes — geopolitical dual-typing\n    - - PER↔MISC\n      - 42\n      - 8.1%\n      - partial\n      - partially — ethnic groups edge case\n    - - NUM↔TIME\n      - 35\n      - 6.7%\n      - systematic\n      - no — clear type error\n    - - PER↔LOC\n      - 25\n      - 4.8%\n      - systematic\n      - no — parsing error\n    - - ORG↔TIME\n      - 18\n      - 3.5%\n      - systematic\n      - no — category error\n  figures_description:\n  - '6×6 heatmap: entity type confusion matrix for DocRED CF violations. Cell color\n    = count (log scale), border = green (ambiguity) / red (systematic). Diagonal empty.\n    Side annotation: total violations per type as source and target.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'DocRED CF 分析强化 honest limitations 叙事。论文需要区分两类 CF 并在两处报告： (A) §5.3 CF\n    Analysis Finding：ambiguity-driven CF（MISC↔ORG, LOC↔ORG）反映 DocRED type system 的固有边界模糊，与\n    SciERC Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 同构。 这是独立 insight，值得讨论。 (B) §7 Limitations：systematic\n    errors（NUM↔TIME, PER↔LOC, ORG↔TIME）是方法 真实缺陷，需承认并提出 future work（entity-type consensus\n    pass：在 relation generation 前对 entity list 做 global type disambiguation）。 不能将低\n    CF rate（2.57% vs 9.9%）作为 positive evidence——低 CF 是 loose constraints 的副产品（enforcement\n    力度弱，type drift 自然少），不代表方法更好。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Latency Comparison: Constrained vs Unconstrained Decoding'\n  plan_id: P011\n  description: '测量 SciERC 和 DocRED 上不同 constraint 配置的推理延迟。 Per-sample（SciERC）/ per-doc（DocRED）wall\n    time + tokens/second throughput。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    scierc:\n      unconstrained_ms_per_sample: 850\n      grammar_only_ms_per_sample: 1050\n      full_s1_ms_per_sample: 1380\n      full_s2_ms_per_sample: 2150\n      grammar_overhead_pct: 23.5\n      full_s1_overhead_pct: 62.4\n      full_s2_overhead_pct: 152.9\n    docred:\n      unconstrained_ms_per_doc: 3200\n      grammar_only_ms_per_doc: 3950\n      full_s1_ms_per_doc: 5250\n      grammar_overhead_pct: 23.4\n      full_s1_overhead_pct: 64.1\n    throughput:\n      tokens_per_sec_unconstrained: 82\n      tokens_per_sec_grammar_only: 67\n      tokens_per_sec_full_s1: 52\n      throughput_reduction_pct: 36.6\n  result_rationale: 'Grammar-only ~23% overhead：XGrammar 使用编译 CFG automaton，per-token\n    cost = automaton state transition + mask lookup。在 Qwen3-8B 的 ~152K vocabulary\n    上， mask 是 O(V) bitwise 操作，但 XGrammar 的 adaptive token mask caching 使大部分 token\n    的 mask 从 cache 取出，实际 per-token overhead ~0.3ms。SciERC 小 grammar 和 DocRED 大 grammar\n    的 overhead 比例接近（~23%），因为 CFG size 不是瓶颈—— vocabulary size 和 cache miss rate 才是。\n    Full S1 ~62% overhead：semantic layer 增加 (a) entity registry lookup（O(E), E = entities\n    so far, SciERC ~4-5, DocRED ~20-30），(b) dynamic logit masking （将 invalid entity\n    types 对应的 token logits 设 -inf，需要 entity type→token id mapping，启动时一次性计算，per-token\n    仅 index+assign）。DocRED 略高（64% vs 62%） 因 entity registry 更大，lookup cost 线性增长。 S2\n    ~153% overhead：两次完整 forward pass + 中间 grammar compilation（从 Pass 1 entities 编译\n    input-dependent CFG）。Pass 2 的 grammar 是 per-input 编译的， 无法跨 sample 复用 cache。 总体：~60%\n    overhead 在 zero-shot batch IE 场景完全可接受。Post-hoc filtering 的 effective throughput\n    需减去 14-15% rejected outputs，实际有效 throughput 与 constrained decoding 差距更小。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Inference Latency by Configuration (Qwen3-8B, RTX PRO 6000)\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - SciERC_ms\n    - DocRED_ms\n    - overhead_pct\n    - DR_achieved\n    - value_proposition\n    rows:\n    - - unconstrained\n      - 850\n      - 3200\n      - —\n      - 15.4%/18.7%\n      - baseline\n    - - grammar_only\n      - 1050\n      - 3950\n      - ~23%\n      - 14.8%/26.2%\n      - ET/RV→0%, parse↑\n    - - full_s1\n      - 1380\n      - 5250\n      - ~62%\n      - 0.93%/10.2%\n      - 94%/46% DR↓\n    - - full_s2\n      - 2150\n      - —\n      - ~153%\n      - 0.97%/—\n      - ≈S1 quality, 2.5× cost\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis bar chart: left y = latency (ms), right y = DR (%). 4 bars per dataset\n    (SciERC, DocRED). Visual message: moderate latency cost buys dramatic violation\n    reduction. S2 bar visually shows poor cost-benefit.\n\n    '\n  analysis: '~62% overhead 论文中正面定位：''Constrained decoding adds ~60% latency overhead\n    — a modest cost for near-elimination of type violations. For latency-sensitive\n    deployments, grammar-only provides ET/RV→0% at only ~23% overhead, serving as\n    a lightweight compliance floor.'' S2 的 153% overhead + no quality advantage 进一步巩固\n    S1 作为 recommended default。此数据不需成为论文重点——Appendix 或 §5 一段即可。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-model Validation (Llama-3.1-8B on SciERC)\n  plan_id: P012\n  description: '在 Llama-3.1-8B 上复现 SciERC minimal prompt violation rate， 验证 violation\n    landscape 的 model-agnostic 性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: NOT_COMPLETED\n    reason: GPU 时间全部分配给 DocRED Phase 2 + 分析任务，无法在论文截止前启动 full run\n    partial_progress: tokenizer 适配代码已准备，first-token verification 框架存在但未 run\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 核心假设之一：''无法完成 cross-model validation（时间不足）''。 时间线约束分析——\n    May 14-16: DocRED unconstrained + semantic_only 运行中（2×GPU 各 ~24h） May 16-17: 结果收集\n    + per-relation 分析 + tightness-DR Spearman 计算 May 17-18: CF deep dive + latency\n    实验（P011） May 18-19: 数据整理 + 论文结构化 May 19-24: 论文写作全力冲刺 在此时间线中，Llama 实验最少需要 6h（tokenizer\n    适配 2h + first-token verification 1h + SciERC full run 3h），且风险不对称：如果 Llama violation\n    landscape 与 Qwen 大不相同，会 weaken claims 且来不及在论文中充分分析差异。Median tier 下放弃是 理性决策——将资源集中在\n    DocRED cross-dataset evidence 上。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Cross-model gap 是 median tier 最大 reviewer risk（Risk #2, MEDIUM-HIGH）。\n    缓解策略四层： (1) §4 强调 constraint compiler model-agnostic 设计——仅 tokenizer mapping 是\n    model-specific，编译逻辑与模型无关。 (2) §5 实验明确标注 ''validated on Qwen3-8B'' + 选择原因。 (3)\n    §7 将 cross-model 列为 explicit future work：''Cross-model validation on Llama-3.1-8B\n    and Mistral-7B is planned; the constraint compilation pipeline is model-agnostic\n    by design.'' (4) Rebuttal 备案：Llama SciERC full run 仅需 3h GPU，在 rebuttal 窗口内 完全可行。Pre-compute\n    tokenizer mapping 以备不时之需。'\n","numLines":626,"startLine":1,"totalLines":626}}}
