{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015amtAB7gyHMj3ECRkTrnAe","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Title\\\\nOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\\\\n(Note: \\\\\\\"Guaranteed\\\\\\\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \\\\\\\"Near-Complete\\\\\\\" is honest and defensible.)\\\\n\\\\n## Core Insight\\\\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero F1 cost** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\\\\n\\\\n**Phase 2 confirmed**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%), and is **F1-neutral** (R-F1 +0.13pp, not statistically significant — correctly framed as \\\\\\\"zero cost\\\\\\\", not \\\\\\\"improvement\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\\\\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\\\\n\\\\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\\\\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\\\\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\\\\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\\\\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\\\\n\\\\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \\\\\\\"5.78% barely above 5%\\\\\\\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\\\\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\\\\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\\\\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\\\\n\\\\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \\\\\\\"synergistic\\\\\\\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\\\\n\\\\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \\\\\\\"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Graceful degradation** (per Reviewer assessment, D008): When $M_{semantic} \\\\\\\\cap M_{grammar} = \\\\\\\\emptyset$ (semantic layer would mask all grammar-valid tokens), the system falls back to grammar-only control. Occurred 1/998 DocRED docs (0.1%), 0/551 SciERC sentences — consistent with tighter constraints increasing empty-intersection likelihood. Implementation is error recovery (fallback), NOT formal invariant guarantee. Do NOT frame as \\\\\\\"provable composition\\\\\\\" — fallback's existence is counter-evidence. Frame as \\\\\\\"engineering robustness\\\\\\\" in §4; mention cross-dataset observation in §5 Discussion (1-2 sentences, N=1 too weak for dedicated analysis).\\\\n\\\\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\\\\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\\\\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\\\\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\\\\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\\\\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\\\\n\\\\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\\\\n\\\\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\\\\n\\\\n### C1: \\\\\\\"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\\\\n\\\\n### C2: \\\\\\\"Why not just post-hoc filter?\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: (a) Post-hoc wastes compute on invalid outputs (14-15% rejection rate); (b) cannot redirect probability mass to valid alternatives; (c) for streaming/real-time extraction, post-hoc filtering is too late. Post-hoc approaches (e.g., SHACL/DL reasoner-based validation, Alviano et al. IJCAI 2025 ASP-based structured knowledge verification) validate constraints after generation but cannot correct invalid outputs during decoding. ⚠️ 原引用 \\\\\\\"LLM+ASP (ICLP 2025)\\\\\\\" 已核实为不准确（venue/方法描述均有误），已修正。\\\\n\\\\n### C3: \\\\\\\"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\\\\n\\\\n### C4: \\\\\\\"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\\\\\\\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\\\\\\\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \\\\\\\"harder instances\\\\\\\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\\\\n\\\\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\\\\n\\\\n### C5: \\\\\\\"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: Phase 0 establishes methodology; cross-model validation (Llama-3.1-8B, 70B quantized) planned for Phase 2 if time permits. The constraint compiler is model-agnostic — only the tokenizer-specific first-token verification needs re-running per model.\\\\n\\\\n### C6: \\\\\\\"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Phase 2 confirms F1-neutral**: S1 R-F1 0.0836 (+0.13pp vs unconstrained 0.0823), S2 R-F1 0.0803 (-0.20pp vs unconstrained). Both within noise on ~1700 triples. Frame as: \\\\\\\"Constraint enforcement is F1-neutral — extraction quality is preserved while violations are near-eliminated.\\\\\\\" Do NOT claim F1 improvement (single seed, no bootstrap CI). Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\\\\n\\\\n### C7: \\\\\\\"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\\\\n\\\\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\\\\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\\\\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\\\\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\\\\n\\\\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\\\\n\\\\n**论证层次**：\\\\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\\\\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\\\\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\\\\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\\\\n\\\\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \\\\\\\"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\\\\\\\" 提供干净的消融证据。\\\\n\\\\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\\\\n\\\\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\\\\n\\\\n### C8: \\\\\\\"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\\\\\\\"\\\\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \\\\\\\"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\\\\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\\\\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\\\\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\\\\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\\\\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\\\\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\\\\n7. Conclusion\\\\n\\\\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\\\\n\\\\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\\\\\\\"\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\\\\\\\"\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\\\\\\\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\\\\\\\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\\\\\\\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\\\\n\\\\n**Claim with caution**:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Near-complete type-valid IE\\\\\\\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \\\\\\\"Near-Complete\\\\\\\"\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\\\\\\\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\\\\n- \\\\\\\"F1 improvement\\\\\\\" — NOT statistically significant, frame as F1-neutral only\\\\n- \\\\\\\"CF reveals type system ambiguity\\\\\\\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\\\\\\\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Do NOT claim**:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"General infrastructure for IE\\\\\\\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\\\\n- \\\\\\\"State-of-the-art\\\\\\\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Synergistic effect\\\\\\\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\\\\n- \\\\\\\"S2 solves CF\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\\\\\\\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Pilot50 DR=0%\\\\\\\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Grammar-first invariant\\\\\\\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\\\\\\\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\\\\n\\\\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\\\\n\\\\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\\\\n2. **Single model limitation** (MEDIUM-HIGH): Only Qwen3-8B tested. Mitigation: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation if time permits.\\\\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \\\\\\\"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\\\\\\\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\\\\n4. **DocRED Phase 2 weak** (MEDIUM): If constrained decoding on DocRED (96 types) shows weaker gains or higher CF, claim generality is weakened.\\\\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral. No longer a risk.\\\\n\\\\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\\\\n\\\\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 complete ✅ + Phase 1 integration ✅\\\\n- **May 14 (now)**: Phase 2 SciERC core results confirmed ✅ (unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1). full_s2 running, DocRED Phase 2 starting.\\\\n- **May 15-17**: DocRED Phase 2 (grammar_only + full_s1) + S2 analysis + CF deep dive + Evaluate-for error cases\\\\n- **May 17-19**: Cross-model (Llama-3.1-8B) if time permits + ablation gaps\\\\n- **May 19-24**: Paper writing (Paper Agent) + submission\\\\n\\\\n**Current bottleneck**: DocRED Phase 2 cross-dataset validation. GPU 0 should be running DocRED grammar_only NOW.\\\\n\\\\n## Status\\\\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\\\\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\\\\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\\\\n- Phase 2 SciERC S1: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓94%, F1-neutral)\\\\n- Phase 2 SciERC S2: ✅ Complete (551/551, DR=0.97%, CF=8.03%, R-F1=8.03% — no advantage over S1)\\\\n- Phase 2 DocRED: 🔄 grammar_only running on cuda:0 (29/998)\\\\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9%, S2 8.03%, both from independent per-relation enforcement)\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 16503, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vaCw2sEZNawuKrG1jNccc","session_id":"7202ddb9-6ca1-4076-af31-515440525a70","uuid":"72a9a111-9d32-4dde-aef6-7e9d4dd53ebb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:51:18.910Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013XhP5BDt6YDWYEETjBvbQ4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: best\n2\tnarrative_guidance: '原始 framing 成立，微调定位。Title 保持 ''Near-Complete''，abstract 明确限定：\n3\t\n4\t  ''near-complete for tightly-constrained ontologies (94% DR reduction on SciERC),\n5\t\n6\t  with predictable partial reduction for complex ontologies (46-55% on DocRED)''。\n7\t\n8\t  核心 novelty 三叉：(1) 首个 violation landscape 系统研究，\n9\t\n10\t  (2) grammar 层完美跨数据集泛化（ET/RV→0%），\n11\t\n12\t  (3) tightness-DR 相关性作为独立 analytical contribution。\n13\t\n14\t  DocRED 10.19% 残留 DR 不是弱点而是 tightness theory 的验证数据点。Claims 无需降级。\n15\t\n16\t  CF rate 在 DocRED 上显著低于 SciERC（~2.6% vs 9.9%），\n17\t\n18\t  进一步支持 \"CF 根因是 type system 模糊性\" 论点。\n19\t\n20\t  '\n21\timagined_experiments:\n22\t- name: DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline\n23\t  plan_id: P_docred_unconstrained\n24\t  description: 'DocRED 998 文档，Phase2 code path 无约束运行。\n25\t\n26\t    验证 Phase2 环境下的 unconstrained DR 与 Phase0 一致（18-20%），\n27\t\n28\t    为计算 DR reduction 提供可比基线。\n29\t\n30\t    '\n31\t  expected_results:\n32\t    documents: 998\n33\t    documents_checked: 962\n34\t    parse_failures: 36\n35\t    json_parse_rate: 0.964\n36\t    total_triples: 16600\n37\t    total_entities: 19200\n38\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.075\n39\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.289\n40\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.19\n41\t    domain_range_violations: 3154\n42\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n43\t    entity_f1: 59.0\n44\t    relation_f1: 8.2\n45\t    relation_precision: 7.0\n46\t    relation_recall: 9.9\n47\t    dr_reduction_full_s1_vs_unconstrained_pct: 46.4\n48\t  result_rationale: 'Phase2 SciERC unconstrained 与 Phase0 完全一致（DR=15.37%），\n49\t\n50\t    证明 Phase2 code path 不引入偏差。DocRED 应同样复现 Phase0 数字。\n51\t\n52\t    DR 预测 19.0%（vs Phase0 18.7%）：Phase2 unconstrained 使用相同 generation 参数，\n53\t\n54\t    但 code path 中的 JSON 后处理可能与 Phase0 略有差异（如 unicode 处理），\n55\t\n56\t    导致少量 triples 解析方式不同，~0.3pp 方差在正常范围。\n57\t\n58\t    Parse rate 保持 ~96.4%——无 grammar 约束时 JSON 格式错误率是模型固有属性。\n59\t\n60\t    RV=28.9% 和 ET=7.5% 复现 Phase0，均为模型在无约束下的自然错误率。\n61\t\n62\t    F1 与 grammar_only(8.24) 和 full_s1(8.17) 持平，确认约束 F1-neutral。\n63\t\n64\t    dr_reduction 46.4% = (19.0-10.19)/19.0，落入 best 档 [46,55] 下界。\n65\t\n66\t    '\n67\t  tables:\n68\t  - 'Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — unconstrained column'\n69\t  - 'Table 1: Cross-dataset Violation Landscape — DocRED Phase2 unconstrained row'\n70\t  figures_description:\n71\t  - 'Figure 4: Enabling dependency grouped bar chart — unconstrained 作为基线参照'\n72\t  analysis: '关键验证点：Phase2 unconstrained DR ≈ Phase0 DR（±1pp），\n73\t\n74\t    确保 reduction 计算分母可比。若偏差 >2pp 需审查 code path 差异。\n75\t\n76\t    46.4% reduction 支持 \"predictable partial reduction for complex ontologies\" 叙事。\n77\t\n78\t    '\n79\t- name: DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only constrained decoding\n80\t  plan_id: P_docred_semantic_only\n81\t  description: '仅启用 semantic 层（TypeConstraintProcessor），不启用 grammar 层。\n82\t\n83\t    验证 enabling dependency 在复杂 ontology 上跨数据集复现：\n84\t\n85\t    无 grammar 保障 relation vocabulary → semantic 层大面积盲区 → DR reduction 显著弱于 full_s1。\n86\t\n87\t    '\n88\t  expected_results:\n89\t    documents: 998\n90\t    documents_checked: 958\n91\t    parse_failures: 40\n92\t    json_parse_rate: 0.96\n93\t    total_triples: 16500\n94\t    total_entities: 19100\n95\t    entity_type_violation_rate: 0.073\n96\t    relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.287\n97\t    domain_range_violation_rate: 0.155\n98\t    domain_range_violations: 2558\n99\t    cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.025\n100\t    entity_f1: 58.5\n101\t    relation_f1: 8.0\n102\t    relation_precision: 6.9\n103\t    relation_recall: 9.5\n104\t    dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct: 18.4\n105\t    semantic_enabling_ratio: 2.52\n106\t  result_rationale: \"Enabling dependency 机制：\\n1. DocRED unconstrained RV=29%，即 ~29%\\\n107\t    \\ triples 使用不在 ontology 中的 relation type。\\n   Semantic 层对这些 triples 完全无法检查——未知\\\n108\t    \\ relation 查不到 domain/range 规则。\\n2. 在剩余 ~71% 合法 relation type 的 triples 中，semantic\\\n109\t    \\ 执行 domain/range 检查。\\n   但无 grammar 结构保障，JSON 解析失败率 ~4%（vs grammar_only 1.5%），\\n\\\n110\t    \\   进一步削弱 semantic 的有效覆盖面。实际 semantic 能检查的 triples 约 67-68%。\\n3. DR 从 19.0% 降至\\\n111\t    \\ 15.5%（-18.4%），远弱于 full_s1 的 46.4%。\\n   SciERC 上 semantic_only reduction=24.2%，DocRED\\\n112\t    \\ 更低（18.4%）正因 RV 更高\\n   （29% vs 1.4%），semantic 盲区更大。\\n4. enabling_ratio = (19.0-10.19)/(19.0-15.5)\\\n113\t    \\ = 8.81/3.5 = 2.52。\\n   Full_s1 的 DR reduction 效力是 semantic_only 的 2.52 倍。\\n\\\n114\t    \\   SciERC ratio=3.88 更高是因为 SciERC full_s1 几乎完全消除了 DR（0.93%）。\\n5. CF 升至 2.5%（vs\\\n115\t    \\ unconstrained ~0.1%），模式与 SciERC semantic_only(2.71%) 一致：\\n   semantic per-relation\\\n116\t    \\ 独立 enforcement 引入跨 relation type 不一致。\\n   DocRED CF 略低因为 DocRED entity types\\\n117\t    \\ 语义边界更清晰。\\n\"\n118\t  tables:\n119\t  - 'Table 3: DocRED Constrained Decoding Ablation — semantic_only column'\n120\t  figures_description:\n121\t  - 'Figure 4: Enabling dependency grouped bar chart — semantic_only 柱明显高于 full_s1'\n122\t  - 'Figure S1 (Appendix): SciERC vs DocRED enabling ratio 对比'\n123\t  analysis: 'enabling_ratio=2.52 在 best 档 [2.0, 3.5] 内。\n124\t\n125\t    与 SciERC(3.88) 对比，DocRED ratio 更低的原因可量化归因于 RV 差异：\n126\t\n127\t    DocRED 29% triples 使用无效 relation（SciERC 仅 1.4%），semantic 盲区面积成比例增大。\n128\t\n129\t    论文核心论述：grammar-enables-semantic 在 ontology 复杂度增加时**更加必要**——\n130\t\n131\t    DocRED 29% RV 使 semantic 层近三分之一 triples 完全无法检查。\n132\t\n133\t    '\n134\t- name: Latency comparison (constrained vs unconstrained)\n135\t  plan_id: P011\n136\t  description: '测量 unconstrained / grammar_only / semantic_only / full_s1 / full_s2\n137\t\n138\t    的 tokens/second 和 wall-clock time，量化约束开销的实用性边界。\n139\t\n140\t    '\n141\t  expected_results:\n142\t    scierc:\n143\t      unconstrained_tok_per_sec: 13.0\n144\t      grammar_only_tok_per_sec: 11.5\n145\t      semantic_only_tok_per_sec: 9.8\n146\t      full_s1_tok_per_sec: 9.5\n147\t      full_s2_tok_per_sec: 6.0\n148\t      overhead_ratio:\n149\t        grammar_only: 1.13\n150\t        semantic_only: 1.33\n151\t        full_s1: 1.37\n152\t        full_s2: 2.17\n153\t    docred:\n154\t      unconstrained_tok_per_sec: 12.5\n155\t      grammar_only_tok_per_sec: 11.0\n156\t      full_s1_tok_per_sec: 9.0\n157\t      overhead_ratio:\n158\t        grammar_only: 1.14\n159\t        full_s1: 1.39\n160\t    wall_clock_per_sample_sec:\n161\t      scierc_unconstrained: 16\n162\t      scierc_full_s1: 22\n163\t      docred_unconstrained: 64\n164\t      docred_full_s1: 89\n165\t  result_rationale: \"1. Grammar-only 开销 ~13%：XGrammar 用 pushdown automaton + C++ backend\\\n166\t    \\ 计算 token mask，\\n   高度优化。文献报告 overhead <10%（Dong et al. 2024），但 IE schema 嵌套结构\\n\\\n167\t    \\   比纯 JSON grammar 复杂（entity list + relation list + nested types），实际稍高。\\n2. Semantic\\\n168\t    \\ 层额外开销 ~20%：TypeConstraintProcessor 是 Python 实现，\\n   每 token 需检查 entity registry\\\n169\t    \\ 状态 + 判断生成位置 + 动态计算 logit mask。\\n   Python GIL 与 GPU inference 的交互是主要瓶颈。\\n3.\\\n170\t    \\ Full_s1 ≈ semantic 开销：bitwise AND 两个 mask 是 O(vocab_size) 操作，\\n   可忽略不计，所以 full_s1\\\n171\t    \\ ≈ max(grammar, semantic) ≈ semantic。\\n4. Full_s2 ~2.2x：两个完整 forward pass，\\n\\\n172\t    \\   Pass 2 还需编译 input-dependent grammar，额外消耗 ~0.1-0.2x。\\n5. DocRED 和 SciERC 的\\\n173\t    \\ overhead ratio 接近（1.37 vs 1.39），\\n   说明开销是 per-token 而非 per-document，与文档长度无关。\\n\"\n174\t  tables:\n175\t  - 'Table 6: Inference Latency Overhead (或 Appendix Table A2)'\n176\t  figures_description:\n177\t  - 'Figure S2 (Appendix): Latency overhead bar chart'\n178\t  analysis: '1.37x overhead 完全可接受。Post-hoc filtering 需重新生成 ~15% 被拒 triples\n179\t\n180\t    （等效 ~1.15x 但无法引导到有效输出，且对 streaming 场景不可用）。\n181\t\n182\t    S2 的 2.2x 开销 + 无质量优势，进一步确认 S1 为推荐策略。\n183\t\n184\t    建议在 §5 用 1 句话报告 overhead，不需单独 section。\n185\t\n186\t    '\n187\t- name: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model violation rate (SciERC)\n188\t  plan_id: P012\n189\t  description: '在 Llama-3.1-8B 上复现 SciERC minimal prompt + 可选 full_s1，\n190\t\n191\t    验证 violation landscape 和 grammar 泛化性的模型无关性。\n192\t\n193\t    '\n194\t  expected_results:\n195\t    unconstrained:\n196\t      total_triples: 1550\n197\t      total_entities: 2200\n198\t      json_parse_rate: 0.98\n199\t      entity_type_violation_rate: 0.006\n200\t      relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.025\n201\t      domain_range_violation_rate: 0.145\n202\t      cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.001\n203\t      relation_f1: 6.5\n204\t      entity_f1: 28.0\n205\t      per_relation_dr:\n206\t        Used-for: 0.005\n207\t        Feature-of: 0.3\n208\t        Compare: 0.38\n209\t        Evaluate-for: 0.22\n210\t        Part-of: 0.2\n211\t        Hyponym-of: 0.12\n212\t        Conjunction: 0.0\n213\t    grammar_only:\n214\t      entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n215\t      relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n216\t      domain_range_violation_rate: 0.14\n217\t    full_s1:\n218\t      entity_type_violation_rate: 0.0\n219\t      relation_vocabulary_violation_rate: 0.0\n220\t      domain_range_violation_rate: 0.012\n221\t      cross_field_consistency_violation_rate: 0.085\n222\t      relation_f1: 6.8\n223\t    cross_model_dr_delta_pp:\n224\t      unconstrained: -0.9\n225\t      full_s1: 0.3\n226\t    per_relation_rank_spearman: 0.89\n227\t  result_rationale: \"1. Llama DR ≈ 14.5%（vs Qwen 15.4%，delta=-0.9pp）：\\n   Violations\\\n228\t    \\ 主要由 ontology constraint structure 驱动。两个 8B 模型在相同 ontology 上\\n   的 violation\\\n229\t    \\ rate 高度相关——差异来源于训练数据分布（Llama 学术文本比例可能不同），\\n   而非根本性的 type assignment 差异。±3pp\\\n230\t    \\ 范围内变动。\\n2. Grammar 层 ET→0%, RV→0%：grammar 约束是 CFG-expressible，\\n   只依赖 tokenizer\\\n231\t    \\ vocabulary mapping。XGrammar 自动适配 Llama 的 SentencePiece tokenizer\\n   （vs Qwen\\\n232\t    \\ 的 tiktoken-based）。ET/RV 消除是 grammar 固有能力，完全模型无关。\\n3. Full_s1 DR ≈ 1.2%（vs Qwen\\\n233\t    \\ 0.93%）：\\n   残留 DR 略高因为 Llama 的 logit distribution 与 Qwen 不同——\\n   semantic mask\\\n234\t    \\ 后次优 token 是否仍违反约束，取决于模型特定的 token 概率排序。\\n   但量级一致（均 <2%），确认方法泛化性。\\n4. F1 略低（6.5\\\n235\t    \\ vs 8.23）：Llama-3.1-8B 在 zero-shot structured output 上\\n   弱于 Qwen3-8B（后者有 code/structured\\\n236\t    \\ output 针对性训练）。不影响约束效果评估。\\n5. Per-relation rank Spearman ρ=0.89：两个模型的 per-relation\\\n237\t    \\ violation 排序\\n   高度一致（Compare > Feature-of > Evaluate-for > ...），因为排序由 constraint\\\n238\t    \\ tightness 驱动。\\n\"\n239\t  tables:\n240\t  - 'Table 5: Cross-model Violation Rate Comparison'\n241\t  figures_description:\n242\t  - 'Figure 5: Cross-model per-relation DR scatter (Qwen x, Llama y), R²>0.75'\n243\t  analysis: '若 per-relation rank Spearman ρ>0.8，可额外 claim：\n244\t\n245\t    \"per-relation violation susceptibility is a property of ontology constraint structure,\n246\t\n247\t    not the generating model\"。Grammar ET/RV→0% 是最干净的跨模型证据。\n248\t\n249\t    注意：P012 是 stretch goal，若时间不足可降级为 appendix 或 future work，\n250\t\n251\t    不影响 core claims。\n252\t\n253\t    '\n254\t- name: DocRED per-relation tightness-DR Spearman correlation\n255\t  plan_id: P_analytical_tightness\n256\t  description: '从 phase2_docred_full_s1 per-relation DR 数据 + DocRED ontology constraint\n257\t    tightness\n258\t\n259\t    计算 Spearman rank correlation。已有 Pearson r=0.3682 (n=90)。\n260\t\n261\t    Spearman ρ 预期更高因为关系为单调非线性。\n262\t\n263\t    '\n264\t  expected_results:\n265\t    pearson_r: 0.3682\n266\t    pearson_r_note: 已实测（来自 root cause analysis）\n267\t    spearman_rho: 0.52\n268\t    spearman_p_value: 2.0e-06\n269\t    n_relations_analyzed: 82\n270\t    filter_criterion: ≥10 triples per relation（排除低频噪声）\n271\t    bucket_level_trend:\n272\t      tightness_0.95_1.00:\n273\t        n_rels: 4\n274\t        agg_dr: 0.306\n275\t      tightness_0.90_0.94:\n276\t        n_rels: 15\n277\t        agg_dr: 0.193\n278\t      tightness_0.85_0.89:\n279\t        n_rels: 28\n280\t        agg_dr: 0.129\n281\t      tightness_0.80_0.84:\n282\t        n_rels: 23\n283\t        agg_dr: 0.07\n284\t      tightness_0.70_0.79:\n285\t        n_rels: 18\n286\t        agg_dr: 0.09\n287\t      tightness_lt_0.70:\n288\t        n_rels: 2\n289\t        agg_dr: 0.007\n290\t    bucket_level_note: Bucket data 已实测（来自 root cause analysis），展示清晰单调趋势\n291\t    top10_violation_concentration: 0.78\n292\t    extreme_relations:\n293\t      P1198_unemployment_rate:\n294\t        tightness: 0.944\n295\t        dr: 0.833\n296\t        n: 6\n297\t      P6_head_of_government:\n298\t        tightness: 0.889\n299\t        dr: 0.846\n300\t        n: 13\n301\t      P35_head_of_state:\n302\t        tightness: 0.889\n303\t        dr: 0.647\n304\t        n: 17\n305\t      P582_end_time:\n306\t        tightness: 0.917\n307\t        dr: 0.435\n308\t        n: 186\n309\t      P205_basin_country:\n310\t        tightness: 0.972\n311\t        dr: 0.37\n312\t        n: 108\n313\t  result_rationale: \"1. Pearson r=0.37 已实测。Spearman ρ 预期更高（~0.52）因为：\\n   (a) 关系是单调但非线性的——bucket\\\n314\t    \\ 数据清晰展示从 0.7% 到 30.6% 的单调上升\\n       （仅 0.70-0.79 bucket 有轻微 inversion，agg_DR=9.0%\\\n315\t    \\ vs 0.80-0.84 的 7.0%）；\\n   (b) Spearman 使用 rank，消除了 DR 右偏分布的 outlier 影响；\\n  \\\n316\t    \\ (c) 过滤 ≥10 triples 排除了低频关系的小样本噪声（这些关系 DR 要么 0% 要么 100%）。\\n2. Pearson r 被低频高\\\n317\t    \\ DR 关系拉低：P1198_unemployment_rate（6 triples, DR=83.3%）\\n   等极端值在 Pearson 下产生高杠杆效应。Spearman\\\n318\t    \\ rank transformation 削弱此影响。\\n3. 0.70-0.79 bucket inversion 的原因：该区间包含 P463_member_of（tightness=0.722,\\n\\\n319\t    \\   DR=9.5%, n=745）——高频关系的 DR 拉高了整个 bucket 的聚合值。\\n   这是个别关系的特性，不破坏整体单调趋势。\\n4.\\\n320\t    \\ ρ=0.52 位于 best 档 [0.5, 0.8] 下端，反映了 tightness 不是 DR 的唯一决定因素：\\n   relation frequency、entity\\\n321\t    \\ type distribution、model-specific prior 也有贡献。\\n   但 tightness 是最强的单一预测因子，ρ=0.52\\\n322\t    \\ 在 n=82 下 p<0.001 显著。\\n\"\n323\t  tables:\n324\t  - 'Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR by Tightness Bucket（已有 bucket 实测数据）'\n325\t  figures_description:\n326\t  - 'Figure 3: Scatter plot — x=tightness, y=full_s1 DR, point_size=log(n_triples).\n327\t    拟合线 + ρ=0.52 annotation. 左下密集聚集（低 tightness, DR≈0%）vs 右上散布（高 tightness, DR 10-85%）'\n328\t  analysis: 'ρ=0.52 + bucket 单调趋势 + top 15 贡献 76.3% violations = 三重证据支持 tightness\n329\t    theory。\n330\t\n331\t    论文 framing：不强调 ρ 的绝对值（0.52 不算 \"strong\"），\n332\t\n333\t    而强调 (a) bucket 趋势的清晰单调性，(b) violation 的极度集中性（top 15 = 76.3%），\n334\t\n335\t    (c) 实用 insight：practitioners 可从 ontology 定义直接预估约束效果。\n336\t\n337\t    Fig 3 scatter plot 是 paper 最重要的 figure 之一——一图讲清核心 story。\n338\t\n339\t    '\n340\t- name: DocRED CF violation root cause analysis\n341\t  plan_id: P_analytical_cf\n342\t  description: '对 phase2_docred_full_s1 的 519 个 CF violations 进行子类型分解，\n343\t\n344\t    与 SciERC CF 模式对比验证 type system ambiguity 假说。\n345\t\n346\t    '\n347\t  expected_results:\n348\t    cf_violations: 519\n349\t    cf_denominator_entities: 20218\n350\t    cf_rate: 0.0257\n351\t    evr_count: 460\n352\t    evr_fraction_of_cf: 0.886\n353\t    evr_entity_rate: 0.023\n354\t    within_rel_count: 50\n355\t    within_rel_fraction: 0.096\n356\t    top_conflict_patterns:\n357\t    - pattern: ORG↔LOC\n358\t      count: 120\n359\t      pct_of_cf: 0.231\n360\t      example: 国家名在 country_of_citizenship 中标 LOC, 在 headquarters 中标 ORG\n361\t    - pattern: PER↔ORG\n362\t      count: 85\n363\t      pct_of_cf: 0.164\n364\t      example: 王朝/政权名在 head_of_state 中标 ORG, 在 instance_of 中标 PER\n365\t    - pattern: TIME↔NUM\n366\t      count: 65\n367\t      pct_of_cf: 0.125\n368\t      example: 年份在 date_of_birth 中标 TIME, 在 P571_inception 中标 NUM\n369\t    ablation_evidence:\n370\t      grammar_only_cf: 14\n371\t      grammar_only_cf_rate: 0.0007\n372\t      full_s1_cf: 519\n373\t      full_s1_cf_rate: 0.0257\n374\t      delta: 505\n375\t      semantic_attribution: 100% — 505/505 增量 CF 来自 semantic 层\n376\t    cross_dataset_comparison:\n377\t      scierc_cf: 0.099\n378\t      docred_cf: 0.026\n379\t      ratio: 3.8\n380\t      explanation: DocRED entity types (PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC) 语义边界远清晰于 SciERC\n381\t        (Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method)\n382\t    trade_off_ratio:\n383\t      dr_reduction_pp: 8.81\n384\t      cf_increase_pp: 2.47\n385\t      benefit_cost: 3.57\n386\t  result_rationale: \"1. CF=2.57% 远低于 SciERC 9.9%：核心原因是 type system 语义清晰度差异。\\n   DocRED\\\n387\t    \\ 的 PER/ORG/LOC/TIME/NUM/MISC 在绝大多数上下文中有明确分类标准\\n   （人名=PER, 组织=ORG, 地名=LOC），边界模糊区域有限（主要是\\\n388\t    \\ ORG↔LOC 的国家实体）。\\n   SciERC 的 Generic/OtherScientificTerm/Material/Method 在学术领域大量重叠\\n\\\n389\t    \\   （\\\"neural network\\\" 可以是 Method 也可以是 OtherScientificTerm）。\\n2. EVR 占 89%（vs\\\n390\t    \\ SciERC >90%）：子类型分布一致。EVR = 同一 entity 在 entity list\\n   和 relation triple 中被赋予不同\\\n391\t    \\ type，根因是 semantic 层按 relation-specific\\n   domain/range 约束选择 type，不维护全局 entity-type\\\n392\t    \\ 一致性。\\n3. ORG↔LOC 是最大冲突模式（23%）：这是 NER 领域公认的困难 case——\\n   国家/城市作为政治实体(ORG) vs\\\n393\t    \\ 地理实体(LOC) 是 type system 设计的固有模糊区。\\n4. Grammar_only CF=14（0.07%）→ full_s1 CF=519（2.57%），增量\\\n394\t    \\ 100% 来自 semantic 层。\\n   干净的消融证据：grammar 不引入 CF，CF 是 semantic type enforcement\\\n395\t    \\ 的系统性副作用。\\n5. Trade-off ratio 3.57:1（每增加 1pp CF 换取 3.57pp DR reduction）。\\n  \\\n396\t    \\ 结合 DR=hard constraint（triple 不可用）vs CF=soft preference（individual triples 仍\\\n397\t    \\ valid），\\n   trade-off 高度有利。DocRED 上比 SciERC（93pp/10pp=9.3:1）差但仍 positive。\\n\"\n398\t  tables:\n399\t  - 'Table 5: CF Analysis — Sub-type Breakdown and Cross-dataset Comparison'\n400\t  figures_description:\n401\t  - 'Figure S3 (Appendix): CF conflict pattern distribution (DocRED vs SciERC 并列)'\n402\t  analysis: 'DocRED CF=2.57% 在 best 档 [2%, 3%] 内。\n403\t\n404\t    Cross-dataset CF 对比（2.57% vs 9.9%）为 \"CF 根因是 type system ambiguity\" 提供强证据：\n405\t\n406\t    type system 边界越模糊 → CF 越高。这个 finding 应在 §5.3 展开（独立 insight 价值），\n407\t\n408\t    同时 §7 保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work（global entity-type consensus）。\n409\t\n410\t    论文绝不能暗示 \"因为 DocRED CF 低所以 CF 问题不重要\"——SciERC 9.9% 仍然 non-trivial。\n411\t\n412\t    '\n413\t- name: Cross-dataset grammar layer generalization verification\n414\t  plan_id: P_analytical_grammar_gen\n415\t  description: '系统性汇总 grammar 层在 SciERC（7 relations）和 DocRED（96 relations）上\n416\t\n417\t    的 ET/RV 消除率，确认完美泛化作为独立贡献。\n418\t\n419\t    '\n420\t  expected_results:\n421\t    scierc_grammar_only:\n422\t      et_violation_rate: 0.0\n423\t      rv_violation_rate: 0.0\n424\t      et_violations: 0\n425\t      rv_violations: 0\n426\t      total_triples: 1725\n427\t    docred_grammar_only:\n428\t      et_violation_rate: 0.0\n429\t      rv_violation_rate: 0.0003\n430\t      et_violations: 0\n431\t      rv_violations: 5\n432\t      total_triples: 17341\n433\t    scierc_full_s1:\n434\t      et_violation_rate: 0.0\n435\t      rv_violation_rate: 0.0\n436\t    docred_full_s1:\n437\t      et_violation_rate: 0.0\n438\t      rv_violation_rate: 0.0003\n439\t    cross_dataset_summary:\n440\t      et_elimination: 100% on both datasets (0/1725 SciERC, 0/17341 DocRED)\n441\t      rv_elimination: 100% SciERC (0/1725), 99.97% DocRED (5/17341)\n442\t      ontology_size_invariance: 7 relations → 96 relations (14x) with no degradation\n443\t  result_rationale: \"1. ET/RV 是 CFG-expressible constraints：entity_type ∈ {valid_types},\\n\\\n444\t    \\   relation_type ∈ {valid_relations}。XGrammar pushdown automaton 可精确 enforce，\\n\\\n445\t    \\   不依赖生成历史或语义状态，因此与模型和 ontology 大小无关。\\n2. SciERC ET=0, RV=0 完美。DocRED ET=0 完美；RV=5/17341=0.03%\\\n446\t    \\ 有微小残留。\\n   这 5 个 RV 可能源于 tokenizer 边界效应——DocRED 某些 relation name\\n   （如 P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction）在\\\n447\t    \\ tokenization 时可能触发 XGrammar\\n   的 token boundary edge case。5/17341 是 noise level，不影响结论。\\n\\\n448\t    3. 从 7 relations 到 96 relations（14x），ET/RV 消除率保持 99.97-100%。\\n   Grammar compilation\\\n449\t    \\ 自动将 ontology schema 转化为 CFG，\\n   schema size 只增加 production rule 数量，不降低 enforcement\\\n450\t    \\ 精确性。\\n4. 数据已全部就位（来自 phase2_scierc_grammar_only 和 phase2_docred_grammar_only），\\n\\\n451\t    \\   这是 compilation + formatting，不需新实验。\\n\"\n452\t  tables:\n453\t  - 'Table 2/3: ET 和 RV 列横跨所有配置和数据集'\n454\t  figures_description:\n455\t  - 无需独立 figure——Table 中 ET/RV 列的 0%/0.03% 已足够说明\n456\t  analysis: 'Grammar 完美泛化是 paper 的 \"clean win\"，无需 caveat。\n457\t\n458\t    建议 §5 第一段就报告此 finding（ET/RV→0% across datasets），\n459\t\n460\t    先给 reviewer 一个 unambiguously positive result，建立信任后再讨论 DR 的 nuance。\n461\t\n462\t    论文可 claim：\"Grammar-constrained decoding is a solved problem for ontology vocabulary\n463\t\n464\t    and entity type compliance in IE—it scales perfectly from 7 to 96 relation types.\"\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t- name: DocRED per-relation DR bimodal distribution analysis\n468\t  plan_id: P_analytical_bimodal\n469\t  description: '分析 96 个 DocRED relations 的 full_s1 per-relation DR 分布形态，\n470\t\n471\t    验证 >65% 关系 DR<2% 的双峰假设。\n472\t\n473\t    '\n474\t  expected_results:\n475\t    total_relations: 96\n476\t    active_relations: 87\n477\t    filter_5plus_triples: 82\n478\t    dr_distribution:\n479\t      dr_eq_0pct: 18\n480\t      dr_lt_2pct: 55\n481\t      dr_2_to_10pct: 12\n482\t      dr_10_to_20pct: 7\n483\t      dr_20_to_40pct: 6\n484\t      dr_gt_40pct: 8\n485\t    near_zero_fraction: 0.67\n486\t    near_zero_fraction_note: 55/82 = 67%（≥5 triples 的 relations 中 DR<2%）\n487\t    distribution_statistics:\n488\t      median_dr: 0.008\n489\t      mean_dr: 0.102\n490\t      mean_median_ratio: 12.75\n491\t      std_dr: 0.18\n492\t      skewness: 2.1\n493\t      gini_coefficient: 0.82\n494\t    top15_concentration: 0.763\n495\t    top15_concentration_note: 已实测：top 15 relations 贡献 1352/1771 = 76.3% 总违规\n496\t  result_rationale: \"1. 67% relations DR<2%（best 档下界 65%）：DocRED 虽然 avg tightness=0.842（高），\\n\\\n497\t    \\   但 tightness 分布也有 variance——0.70-0.84 区间的 41 个 relations 中，\\n   许多的实际 DR 较低是因为\\\n498\t    \\ (a) 高频 entity types（PER, ORG, LOC）自然匹配这些 relation\\n   的 domain/range，(b) 模型的\\\n499\t    \\ distributional prior 与 ontology 约束高度对齐。\\n   仅在 tightness 极高（>0.90）时，prior-constraint\\\n500\t    \\ mismatch 才产生显著 DR。\\n2. Mean>>Median（12.75x）：经典 heavy-tail 特征。\\n   8 个 DR>40%\\\n501\t    \\ 的 extreme relations（P1198, P6, P171, P35 等，全部 tightness>0.88）\\n   将 mean 拉至\\\n502\t    \\ 10.2%（= overall 10.19%），但 median 0.8% 代表 \\\"典型\\\" relation 体验。\\n3. Gini=0.82：violation\\\n503\t    \\ 分布极不平等。类比帕累托法则：~12% 的 relations 贡献 ~80% violations。\\n   这不是随机噪声，而是 ontology\\\n504\t    \\ constraint structure 的系统性产物。\\n4. 双峰形成机制：constraint tightness 作为 bifurcation\\\n505\t    \\ parameter——\\n   tightness < ~0.80 时 semantic mask 只排除少量 low-probability tokens，\\n\\\n506\t    \\   model 自然分布已近乎合法，DR→0%（左峰）；\\n   tightness > ~0.90 时 mask 必须排除 high-probability\\\n507\t    \\ tokens，\\n   model 被迫使用低概率 token，DR 急剧上升（右尾）。\\n   0.80-0.90 是 transition zone，DR\\\n508\t    \\ 分散，中间 bin 较薄。\\n\"\n509\t  tables:\n510\t  - 'Table 4: DocRED Per-relation DR Summary Statistics'\n511\t  figures_description:\n512\t  - 'Figure 2: Histogram — 96 relations 的 full_s1 DR 分布. 左峰 (0-2%, ~55 relations)\n513\t    显著高于右尾 (>20%, ~14 relations). Vertical dashed line at DR=2%. Inset: log-scale\n514\t    清晰展示右尾结构'\n515\t  analysis: 'near_zero_fraction=67% 在 best 档 [65%, 80%] 下端。\n516\t\n517\t    这个分布图的论文价值：visually 传达 \"10.19% overall DR 不是均匀分布的失败\"——\n518\t\n519\t    对 2/3 的 relations，constrained decoding 已实现 near-complete compliance；\n520\t\n521\t    残留 DR 集中在可预测的少数 high-tightness relations。\n522\t\n523\t    Fig 2 + Fig 3 (tightness scatter) 构成核心 evidence pair：\n524\t\n525\t    分布展示现象（双峰），scatter 解释机制（tightness 驱动）。'\n526\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQJgxK6mXbaBdupN9NUdYe","session_id":"7202ddb9-6ca1-4076-af31-515440525a70","uuid":"889b7b1f-6cd1-4001-9a02-a271313dedbe","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:51:18.775Z"}
